#: ../../source/docs/xbee-radios.rst:91
#: 80909836e3a84d9baaa05ef39d3dad64
msgid "(Optional) Changing your telemetry to use UART2 (aka Serial3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/xbee-radios.rst:93
#: 242a3bd49205499683403e39c2c2b464
msgid "By default an Xbee connected to the APM2 will use UART0 (aka \"Serial\" in Arduino) which is shared with the USB as mentioned above. If you wish to instead use UART2 (aka \"Serial3\") for telemetry you can change the \"AutoMUX UART0\" jumper on the bottom of the APM2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/xbee-radios.rst:98
#: b99ac4f6969945ce91f6e5d5ea9e0e97
msgid "Although difficult to see, by default there are two small jumpers between the upper pads that must be cut with an X-Acto blade. Then a new solder bridge must be made to join the bottom pads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/xbee-radios.rst:106
#: 5cf999de4a3640c28bdf774cc4d3cbcc
msgid "(Optional) Rolling your own Xbee telemetry setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/xbee-radios.rst:108
#: 780807ea53884219adf6c6305fbe758f
msgid "You can make your own telemetry kit if you'd like. The first thing to keep in mind is that you should use Xbee modules in a different frequency range than your RC equipment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/xbee-radios.rst:112
#: c5bcabdd745c4e01a63fd35189840af0
msgid "In general, we recommend 900Mhz Xbee modules, but in some countries 900Mhz is not approved. In those cases you can use 2.4Ghz Xbee modules. In that configuration, we use *Xbee Pro wireless modules*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/xbee-radios.rst:116
#: 19425c01dd814cc38c5f2ef679bf7b05
msgid "Setup can be a little tricky, so please see the comments below in this manual to see how other people have done it. In particular, we do not recommend the DIY Drones XtreamBee adapter for those modules. Instead, try the"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/xbee-radios.rst:121
#: 853a5831b8e1470d8e9181a4f1159c2b
msgid "`Sparkfun <https://www.sparkfun.com/categories/111>`__ adapters. Please note that the DIY Drones team will only support the recommended 900Mhz Xbee modules, so if you use something else please turn the community for help, not the DIY Drones developers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/xbee-radios.rst:126
#: e5b736a992e743f48b52a3341cd3288e
msgid "`Here is more discussion <https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/some-tips-on-picking-frequencies>`__ on how to pick the best frequencies for your setup."
msgstr ""

